## 2. nfl_data_py (nflverse) — the data-access layer

Repo at `/workspace/repos/nfl_data_py`. **NB: archived Sep 2025 → migrate upstream to
`nflreadpy`.** The API surface here is the *contract* to preserve.

### 2.1 Edge methodology
Pure data plumbing — but the *data choices* define the edge surface. Functions:
`import_pbp_data`, `import_weekly_data`, `import_seasonal_data`, `import_snap_counts`,
`import_ngs_data`, `import_qbr` (NFL+college), `import_seasonal_pfr` / `import_weekly_pfr`,
`import_officials`, `import_schedules`, `import_seasonal_rosters`,
`import_weekly_rosters`, `import_players`, `import_depth_charts`, `import_injuries`,
`import_ids`, `import_contracts`, `import_win_totals`, `import_sc_lines`, `import_draft_picks`,
`import_draft_values`, `import_combine_data`, `import_ftn_data`, plus `clean_nfl_data`
(aligns name diffs for merges) and `cache_pbp`.

### 2.2 Data pipeline — source endpoints (parquet/CSV directly from nflverse releases)
| Dataset | Source URL (template) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| play-by-play | `nflverse-data/releases/.../pbp/play_by_play_{year}.parquet` (1999+) | also participation `pbp_participation_{year}.parquet` |
| weekly player | `nflverse-data/.../player_stats/player_stats_{year}.parquet` | incl. target share, air-yards, dominator |
| players / teams | `.../players/players.parquet`; `nflfastR-data/.../teams_colors_logos.csv` | canonical IDs, team colors/logos |
| weekly rosters | `nflverse-data/.../rosters/roster_{year}.parquet` (via import_weekly_rosters) | in-season updates |
| depth charts | `.../depth_charts_{year}.parquet` | starter identification |
| injuries | `.../injuries_{year}.parquet` | game-time decision flags |
| NGS (speed) | `.../ngs_{year}.parquet` | YAC, air yards, route data |
| PFR adv stats | `advstats_season_{s_type}.parquet`; `advstats_week_{year}_{wk}.parquet` | DVOA proxies |
| snap counts | `.../snap_counts_{year}.parquet` | volume confirmation |
| schedules | `http://www.habitatring.com/games.csv` (all years, filter in-memory) |
| odds / lines | `mrcaseb/nfl-data/.../nfl_lines_odds.csv.gz` | closing lines, win totals |
| sc_lines | `nfldata/.../sc_lines.csv` | |
| win totals | `.../win_totals` (see warning) | data source currently broken per code |
| QBR | `espnscrapeR-data/.../qbr-{year}-{season_type}.csv` | |
| player-id map | `dynastyprocess/data/.../db_playerids.csv` | cross-site ID resolution |
| draft picks/values | `.../draft_picks.parquet`, `.../draft_values.csv` | |
| combine | `.../combine.parquet` | |
| FTN charting | `.../ftn_charting_{year}.parquet` | route-level detail |
| officials | `nfldata/.../officials.csv` | |

Patterns (all importers): single-threaded `pandas.read_parquet/csv` per year; optional
`cache=True` via `appdirs.user_cache_dir('nfl_data_py','cooper_dff')`; `thread_requests=True`
switches some to `ThreadPoolExecutor`. `downcast=True` converts float64→float32 (memory).
`clean_nfl_data` aligns name diffs so weekly↔pbp↔pfr joins are consistent.

### 2.3 Reusable code
- The full endpoint template list + caching pattern (copy into any re-implementation).
- `clean_nfl_data` name-alignment for cross-source joins.
- Replace `import_*` → `nflreadpy.load_*` when migrating (same nflverse backends; Polars by
  default, `.to_pandas()` available).

