## 4. draftkings_api_explorer (yzRobo) — the DK feed scraper

Repo at `/workspace/repos/draftkings_api_explorer`. The most polished, defensive scraper of the
four. Single-file `dk_api_gui_explorer.py` (62KB).

### 4.1 Edge methodology
- **Main-line detection** (`apply_smart_formatting`): DK returns *every* alternate line as a
  separate Over/Under selection. The code pivots Over/Under into one row per participant per
  line, then for each participant selects the **main line via DK's own `main` flag**, falling
  back to a `cost = |OverOdds|+|UnderOdds|` minimum (closest to -110) when the flag is absent.
  Comment: *"the cost heuristic is only a fallback ... it does get the line wrong when an
  adjacent alternate happens to be priced marginally tighter than the real line."* → use `main`
  flag, not cost, as authoritative.
- **"Uncorrelated parlay edge" data** (H0 Edge 1): the explorer pivots player props so
  `Subject/Line/Over Odds/Under Odds` are directly joinable with internal projection
  distributions to compute true joint probabilities vs. SGP payouts.

### 4.2 Data pipeline
```python
DEFAULT_API_BASE = "https://sportsbook-nash.draftkings.com/api/sportscontent/dkusoh/v1"
DEFAULT_LEAGUE_ID = "88808"   # NFL
build_api_url(league_id, category_id, subcategory_id)   # /leagues/{id}/categories/{c}[/subcategories/{s}]
fetch_dk_feed(...) -> cffi_requests.get(..., impersonate="chrome110", timeout=30)
```
Key defensive choices:
- Uses **`curl_cffi.requests`** with `impersonate="chrome110"` — browser TLS/UA impersonation to
  bypass DK bot detection (far more reliable than `requests`).
- `StructureAnalyzer` + `EnhancedDynamicParser` — analyzes unknown feed shapes dynamically
  (market/selection field patterns, label patterns, participant-extraction from market names via
  regex). Market-type auto-detected by label ratios: if >80% Over/Under → `over_under`/`player_props`
  (category 1759 = player_props); ordinals 1st-4th → `division_standings` (820); labels ending `+`
  → `threshold` (1801 = rookie props).
- Feed normalization: `normalize_market_name` strips DK's `"NFL 2026/27 - "` prefix;
  `resolve_outcome` handles the combined `"Over 3949.5"` label vs. separate `points` field.
- `id_reference.json` — **bundled NFL category/subcategory ID reference** (15 futures groups:
  WIN(1286), FUTURES(529), AWARDS(787), MOST DRAFT..., plus REGION 49808 = NFL; category 1759 =
  Player Props, 1801 = Rookie/Total Props, 820 = Division Standings).
- SHA-256 verified auto-updater: fetches latest GitHub release, verifies asset `digest` starts
  with `sha256:`, size + hash match, atomic same-volume rename (Windows can't overwrite running
  .exe → moves current to `.old`, deleted next launch).
- Threading: scrape runs in a worker thread; `queue.Queue` for log + UI updates; `root.after` poller.

### 4.3 Reusable code
- `curl_cffi` + `impersonate="chrome110"` HTTP pattern (anti-bot bypass) — **the single most
  portable win**.
- `build_api_url` / `fetch_dk_feed` minimal DK feed client (~15 lines, no GUI).
- `StructureAnalyzer` + `EnhancedDynamicParser` + `apply_smart_formatting` — generic
  "analyze-then-parse unknown sportsbook feed" pattern.
- `normalize_market_name` / `resolve_outcome` regexes (handle prefix + embedded-line labels).
- Main-line selection logic (prefer `main` flag; cost heuristic fallback).
- Verified-update pattern (SHA-256 + size check + atomic rename).

