## Cross-repo capability matrix

| Capability | nflalgorithm | nfl_data_py | LuckyLines | DK Explorer |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Data ingestion** | nflreadpy (full feature set) | nflverse parquet/CSV (raw) | DK + OddsAPI/SQL | DK feed only |
| **Projection model** | position-specific ML (separate) | none (data only) | XGBoost/LGBM/LSTM ensemble | none |
| **Odds source** | The Odds API | nfl_lines_odds.csv (closing) | DK + OddsAPI | DK live feed (main-line aware) |
| **Value math** | no-vig + Kelly + normal CDF | none | EV% via normal CDF | none (data layer) |
| **Confidence sizing** | 4-tier 0-100 multi-factor | none | none | none |
| **Correlation/risk** | corr-group + Monte Carlo Kelly | none | DFS stacking (QB-WR) | none |
| **Optimization** | none | none | OR-Tools DFS optimizer | none |
| **Steam/momentum agent** | `odds_agent` (line movement) | none | none | provides raw line snapshots |
| **Reusable scraper** | — | — | — | yes (best quality) |

### Recommended integration path (parent project)
1. Take the **DK Explorer's `fetch_dk_feed` + main-line pivot** as the live odds feed
   (replace LuckyLines' DK ingestion and nflalgorithm's Odds-API-only props).
2. Use **nfl_data_py's endpoint list** (migrated to `nflreadpy`) as the *data backbone* for
   training features; bolt on LuckyLines' **feature_engineering.py** (EMA/lag/streak/vegas/defense/weather) for the X.
3. Compute value with the **shared no-vig + normal-CDF + Kelly** logic (cross-check
   nflalgorithm vs. LuckyLines STD_DEV per market).
4. Size via nflalgorithm's **confidence tiers** + **correlation-aware Kelly**; run LuckyLines'
   **OR-Tools optimizer** for DFS construction.
5. Add nflalgorithm's **`odds_agent` + `market_bias_agent`** as live-monitoring/edge triggers.

